WEBVTT

00:02:28.171 --> 00:02:31.408
It was a slow-moving
wreck in my career itself.

00:02:31.432 --> 00:02:32.862
I was in decline.

00:02:32.886 --> 00:02:34.187
Finally had to pack it in.

00:02:34.211 --> 00:02:37.135
I had to admit it to myself
that I wasn't the horn player

00:02:37.159 --> 00:02:38.618
I had always dreamed of being.

00:02:38.642 --> 00:02:40.745
And right now,
I'm talking about it with you

00:02:40.769 --> 00:02:42.864
and, you know,
we're laughing and all that,

00:02:42.888 --> 00:02:45.507
but I've got to tell you,
it kills me, I still hate it.

00:02:45.531 --> 00:02:47.689
AG: Arthur didn't plan
to quit music so early.

00:02:47.713 --> 00:02:50.633
He simply stopped being great at his job.

00:02:50.657 --> 00:02:53.276
And in the years since,
it's made him wonder,

00:02:53.300 --> 00:02:56.351
does career decline happened
to all of us eventually?

00:02:56.375 --> 00:02:58.411
And is there anything we can do about it?

00:02:58.435 --> 00:03:04.954
(Music)